1
00:00:29,880 --> 00:00:31,420
Paradise

2
00:00:59,140 --> 00:01:02,400
targets I'm waiting
for you to wait for you

3
00:01:07,440 --> 00:01:09,977
It's my heart, my heart,

4
00:01:10,060 --> 00:01:14,917
my heart I'm waiting for
you to come back I'm going

5
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:18,360
to go back to the next day
I'm going to battle for you

6
00:01:57,913 --> 00:01:59,317
I have special powers, too,
and he's coming for me.

7
00:01:59,400 --> 00:02:02,871
Well, why did I have to be the
one with the crest of light?

8
00:02:10,260 --> 00:02:11,380
Great party, huh?

9
00:02:11,660 --> 00:02:13,719
Yeah, Mimi throws the best parties.

10
00:02:15,160 --> 00:02:16,513
Hey, Suzy, wanna dance?

11
00:02:16,980 --> 00:02:18,040
Great, let's go.

12
00:02:18,380 --> 00:02:19,777
We had a great time, Mimi.

13
00:02:19,860 --> 00:02:20,777
See you tomorrow.

14
00:02:20,860 --> 00:02:21,820
OK, see ya.

15
00:02:25,120 --> 00:02:25,950
Daddy!

16
00:02:28,200 --> 00:02:29,030
Hmm.

17
00:02:29,113 --> 00:02:29,943
I just don't get it.

18
00:02:30,026 --> 00:02:33,817
We've never been able to travel to the
digital world without our digivices or D3s,

19
00:02:33,900 --> 00:02:35,860
but somehow, Kari did.

20
00:02:36,260 --> 00:02:38,640
And not only did she not have her D3,

21
00:02:38,880 --> 00:02:42,233
she was transported there
without going through any gate.

22
00:02:42,680 --> 00:02:46,097
There must be something special
about Kari that we're not aware of.

23
00:02:46,180 --> 00:02:47,440
Huh? An email?

24
00:02:49,280 --> 00:02:50,180
It's from Yoli.

25
00:02:50,440 --> 00:02:51,617
There's a digi-egg nearby.

26
00:02:51,700 --> 00:02:53,097
We're going to keep cooking.

27
00:02:53,180 --> 00:02:54,257
Going to keep cooking?

28
00:02:54,340 --> 00:02:57,575
Well, whatever you're making,
be sure and save me some.

29
00:02:58,340 --> 00:02:59,580
Sorry, it was a typo.

30
00:02:59,700 --> 00:03:02,277
We're going to keep
looking That sounds good.

31
00:03:02,360 --> 00:03:06,595
There are no control spires in that
area, so feel free to take your time

32
00:03:07,800 --> 00:03:08,630
Hmm?

33
00:03:08,713 --> 00:03:10,560
Whoa, a digiport is opened in America

34
00:03:11,120 --> 00:03:12,820
Hey, wait, Mimi lives there

35
00:03:13,760 --> 00:03:15,257
But it's not even morning there yet.

36
00:03:15,340 --> 00:03:17,340
I can't call her Let's see.

37
00:03:17,840 --> 00:03:19,134
I'll send her an email

38
00:03:21,240 --> 00:03:22,900
I can't walk another step.

39
00:03:23,380 --> 00:03:26,337
I gotta eat something now Yeah,
I'm getting kind of hungry,

40
00:03:26,420 --> 00:03:29,397
too But we're very close to
finding the new digi-egg.

41
00:03:29,480 --> 00:03:31,717
When we find that digi-egg,
I'm going to eat it.

42
00:03:31,800 --> 00:03:35,682
You'll do no such thing, and
besides, your cholesterol's too high.

43
00:03:36,360 --> 00:03:38,857
Well, if we want to eat,
we'll have to go back.

44
00:03:38,940 --> 00:03:39,977
Sounds good to me.

45
00:03:40,060 --> 00:03:42,120
So long, digi-egg. Hey, look.

46
00:03:42,720 --> 00:03:45,637
On the other side of the lake,
I think it's a restaurant.

47
00:03:45,720 --> 00:03:46,550
A restaurant?

48
00:03:46,740 --> 00:03:47,917
We'll save the glass.

49
00:03:48,000 --> 00:03:51,897
Would you like to sit in the
digivolving or Digivolving section?

50
00:03:51,980 --> 00:03:54,380
Ah, that was delicious. Oh,

51
00:03:54,820 --> 00:03:58,477
I'm going to recommend this restaurant to
all my friends who dine in the Digi World.

52
00:03:58,560 --> 00:04:00,520
Yeah, me too. What's wrong, TK?

53
00:04:01,360 --> 00:04:03,837
Something about this place
is really bothering me.

54
00:04:03,920 --> 00:04:06,397
I feel like I've been here
before and it wasn't good.

55
00:04:06,480 --> 00:04:08,857
Maybe the last time you were
here, you ordered the wrong thing.

56
00:04:08,940 --> 00:04:09,999
Excuse me, waiter.

57
00:04:10,140 --> 00:04:11,437
We're ready for our check, please.

58
00:04:11,520 --> 00:04:12,940
Okay, hold your horses.

59
00:04:13,200 --> 00:04:15,259
After all, I've only got one shell.

60
00:04:16,540 --> 00:04:17,952
What's our bill come to?

61
00:04:18,060 --> 00:04:20,757
$87 Digi Dollars plus tip. Huh?

62
00:04:20,840 --> 00:04:22,240
What's the problem?

63
00:04:22,620 --> 00:04:24,091
Don't you have any money?

64
00:04:24,800 --> 00:04:28,094
We don't have Digi-Dollars,
but we have plenty of money.

65
00:04:28,460 --> 00:04:30,260
But our money's just as good.

66
00:04:30,440 --> 00:04:33,617
Since the Dark Masters left,
we only accept Digi-Dollars.

67
00:04:33,700 --> 00:04:34,677
What's the problem?

68
00:04:34,760 --> 00:04:36,557
The lunk-headed waiter
won't take my money.

69
00:04:36,640 --> 00:04:37,470
Uh-oh.

70
00:04:37,553 --> 00:04:39,137
I see you're being your usual blunt self.

71
00:04:39,220 --> 00:04:40,597
I'm just trying to be honest.

72
00:04:40,680 --> 00:04:43,197
I think you kids are trying
to skip out on the bill.

73
00:04:43,280 --> 00:04:45,080
I told you, we have $87.

74
00:04:45,660 --> 00:04:48,817
Only Digi-Dollars or the
Digi-Express card. That's it.

75
00:04:48,900 --> 00:04:51,137
I'm not going to recommend
this restaurant to anyone.

76
00:04:51,220 --> 00:04:52,050
Good.

77
00:04:52,133 --> 00:04:53,917
I don't want any human
world deadbeats in here.

78
00:04:54,000 --> 00:04:56,176
No wonder the French detest tourists.

79
00:04:56,800 --> 00:05:00,277
Now are you going to work off your
bill or do I have to call a cop?

80
00:05:00,360 --> 00:05:02,617
I think I've heard
something like this before.

81
00:05:02,700 --> 00:05:04,817
If we work here, we'll
be late getting home.

82
00:05:04,900 --> 00:05:06,557
Can't we just pay the
next time we're here?

83
00:05:06,640 --> 00:05:08,097
There won't be a next time.

84
00:05:08,180 --> 00:05:09,717
You're not allowed in here again.

85
00:05:09,800 --> 00:05:12,557
Now get in that kitchen and
start washing dishes or I'll...

86
00:05:12,640 --> 00:05:13,470
Fear not.

87
00:05:13,553 --> 00:05:14,576
I'll pay their bill.

88
00:05:14,980 --> 00:05:15,860
How sweet.

89
00:05:16,100 --> 00:05:17,820
Prince Charming. Who are you?

90
00:05:17,940 --> 00:05:18,770
This is Michael.

91
00:05:18,853 --> 00:05:21,377
He's a friend of mine I
brought with me from America.

92
00:05:21,460 --> 00:05:22,290
It's Mimi.

93
00:05:23,160 --> 00:05:25,397
Oh, Mimi, it's so good to see you again.

94
00:05:25,480 --> 00:05:27,117
What are you doing here in the DigiWorld?

95
00:05:27,200 --> 00:05:30,177
Izzy sent me an email saying there
was a DigiPort open in America,

96
00:05:30,260 --> 00:05:33,557
so I thought it would be a great
opportunity to come visit everyone.

97
00:05:33,640 --> 00:05:36,777
And since Michael's a good friend of
mine, I thought I'd bring him along.

98
00:05:36,860 --> 00:05:39,937
And I want everyone here to say
hello to a good friend of mine, too.

99
00:05:40,020 --> 00:05:40,850
Pleased to meet you.

100
00:05:40,933 --> 00:05:41,960
My name's Betamon.

101
00:05:43,120 --> 00:05:44,457
Betamon is really cool.

102
00:05:44,540 --> 00:05:49,128
He lives in the water and uses his beta
slugger attack to wipe out his enemies

103
00:05:49,340 --> 00:05:51,957
Hey, Palmon, are you sure
it's okay that you're here?

104
00:05:52,040 --> 00:05:53,797
What about the area you're protecting?

105
00:05:53,880 --> 00:05:54,710
No problem,

106
00:05:54,793 --> 00:05:56,477
Tentomon said he'd watch
it for me if I brought him

107
00:05:56,560 --> 00:05:59,077
back a souvenir t-shirt I
don't understand something,

108
00:05:59,160 --> 00:06:02,017
Mimi How are you able to bring
Michael to the digital world?

109
00:06:02,100 --> 00:06:06,920
Oh, that's easy I forgot to tell you,
Michael has a Digivice just like us Huh?

110
00:06:07,400 --> 00:06:08,260
Wait a minute

111
00:06:08,920 --> 00:06:12,357
If he has a Digivice, then he's
a Digidestined That's right,

112
00:06:12,440 --> 00:06:15,337
and his Digivice is the same
kind as mine and the others.

113
00:06:15,420 --> 00:06:17,817
So he became a Digidestined in America at

114
00:06:17,900 --> 00:06:20,457
the same time our original
group did in Japan.

115
00:06:20,540 --> 00:06:21,897
Tell us something, Michael.

116
00:06:21,980 --> 00:06:24,257
Are there more Digidestined
kids like you in America?

117
00:06:24,340 --> 00:06:27,157
And tell us how you became a
Digidestined in the first place.

118
00:06:27,240 --> 00:06:29,100
And tell me you're single. Huh?

119
00:06:29,320 --> 00:06:31,297
All I know is everything
happened four summers

120
00:06:31,380 --> 00:06:33,297
ago when I first saw
Gorilla Mon in New York.

121
00:06:33,380 --> 00:06:36,097
I thought it was simply another ape
climbing the Empire State Building.

122
00:06:36,180 --> 00:06:39,197
That's the same time my Otis
Mon was taking over Tokyo.

123
00:06:39,280 --> 00:06:40,110
TK's right.

124
00:06:40,340 --> 00:06:41,458
My, that's strange.

125
00:06:41,560 --> 00:06:43,397
I wonder if that means
we all had an encounter

126
00:06:43,480 --> 00:06:45,697
with the Digimon at the exact same time.

127
00:06:45,780 --> 00:06:46,660
It's possible.

128
00:06:47,360 --> 00:06:49,037
That's when I was on
that airplane that had

129
00:06:49,120 --> 00:06:50,957
to make an emergency landing in the water.

130
00:06:51,040 --> 00:06:54,097
I didn't know it then, but that's
when I saw my first Digimon.

131
00:06:54,180 --> 00:06:55,577
I remember that, Summer.

132
00:06:55,660 --> 00:06:59,297
I was one of the people being held at
the convention center by the Bakemon.

133
00:06:59,380 --> 00:07:00,997
I wish I could say that Summer was as

134
00:07:01,080 --> 00:07:03,117
terrifying for me as it
was for all of you guys,

135
00:07:03,200 --> 00:07:04,837
but it wasn't because nothing happened.

136
00:07:04,920 --> 00:07:08,637
Although I did send a bunch of emails
during the battle with Diaboramon.

137
00:07:08,720 --> 00:07:10,955
So then everyone was involved somehow.

138
00:07:11,560 --> 00:07:12,857
It's like we're all connected.

139
00:07:12,940 --> 00:07:14,764
But there's still one question.

140
00:07:15,060 --> 00:07:16,707
Who's going to pay the bill?

141
00:07:16,940 --> 00:07:18,097
Don't worry about it.

142
00:07:18,180 --> 00:07:19,537
The entire meal is on me.

143
00:07:19,620 --> 00:07:20,450
That's it.

144
00:07:20,533 --> 00:07:22,064
Now I remember where I saw him.

145
00:07:23,480 --> 00:07:25,917
He used to be one of
Myotismond's henchmen.

146
00:07:26,000 --> 00:07:28,177
He made Matt and Joe
work in the kitchen here.

147
00:07:28,260 --> 00:07:32,097
He got really mad when Matt asked if
he could get half price on his meals.

148
00:07:32,180 --> 00:07:34,857
I can't believe he used
to be one of the bad guys.

149
00:07:34,940 --> 00:07:38,057
All right, I admit it, that was a
rotten egg, but that was in the past.

150
00:07:38,140 --> 00:07:41,657
After the Dark Masters were all defeated,
I knew I had to break out of my shell.

151
00:07:41,740 --> 00:07:42,916
I'm a whole new man.

152
00:07:43,040 --> 00:07:45,677
We're all very proud of you
since you changed your ways.

153
00:07:45,760 --> 00:07:48,037
And don't you feel a lot
better about yourself?

154
00:07:48,120 --> 00:07:52,277
Well, now that you mention it, it is
kind of nice making an honest living.

155
00:07:52,360 --> 00:07:55,657
It seems to me you're still one of the
bad guys after the way you treated me.

156
00:07:55,740 --> 00:07:56,570
Come on, Yoli.

157
00:07:56,680 --> 00:07:58,077
Everyone gets a little cranky.

158
00:07:58,160 --> 00:08:00,117
If he says he's changed, I believe him.

159
00:08:00,200 --> 00:08:01,317
I guess you're right.

160
00:08:01,400 --> 00:08:03,677
Sometimes it's easy to
get cranky with you.

161
00:08:03,760 --> 00:08:06,557
Gee, I really feel pretty bad
about how I treated you last time.

162
00:08:06,640 --> 00:08:08,057
He had a change of heart, huh?

163
00:08:08,140 --> 00:08:08,970
Huh?

164
00:08:09,053 --> 00:08:12,037
Well, it didn't seem like that when he was
yelling at us for trying to eat and run.

165
00:08:12,120 --> 00:08:14,717
But I guess I'll give him
the benefit of the doubt.

166
00:08:14,800 --> 00:08:16,520
It's okay, Digitamamon.

167
00:08:16,660 --> 00:08:19,131
I'm sure you're not a total loser anymore.

168
00:08:19,540 --> 00:08:20,370
Huh?

169
00:08:20,453 --> 00:08:21,297
I don't want your pity.

170
00:08:21,380 --> 00:08:22,397
I want your money.

171
00:08:22,480 --> 00:08:25,780
Work it over now. Huh?
Relax. Don't get upset.

172
00:08:25,940 --> 00:08:27,657
She was just trying to
make you feel better.

173
00:08:27,740 --> 00:08:28,570
Right, Yoli?

174
00:08:28,653 --> 00:08:29,620
Um, yeah.

175
00:08:29,900 --> 00:08:31,757
Besides, we always
intended to pay the bill.

176
00:08:31,840 --> 00:08:32,877
If you would have been more patient,

177
00:08:32,960 --> 00:08:34,737
we probably could have
avoided this whole thing.

178
00:08:34,820 --> 00:08:35,650
You're right.

179
00:08:35,733 --> 00:08:36,563
I'm sorry.

180
00:08:36,646 --> 00:08:37,757
My brains have been scrambled lately.

181
00:08:37,840 --> 00:08:39,237
I've got to look at the sunny side.

182
00:08:39,320 --> 00:08:40,150
I've got a good job.

183
00:08:40,233 --> 00:08:41,137
I've got my health.

184
00:08:41,220 --> 00:08:42,717
And someday I might even have friends.

185
00:08:42,800 --> 00:08:43,917
Tell you what, forget the bill.

186
00:08:44,000 --> 00:08:44,830
It's on me.

187
00:08:45,020 --> 00:08:45,857
You know, Mimi,

188
00:08:45,940 --> 00:08:49,857
I admire you because no matter who you
meet, you bring out the best in everyone.

189
00:08:49,940 --> 00:08:51,097
You're really special.

190
00:08:51,180 --> 00:08:53,298
Plus, I saved you some Digi-Dollars.

191
00:08:54,540 --> 00:08:56,577
Looks like someone has a crush on Mimi.

192
00:08:56,660 --> 00:08:58,677
Looks like someone has a crush on Mimi.

193
00:08:58,760 --> 00:09:00,760
How come I never get the cute guy?

194
00:09:03,480 --> 00:09:05,460
It must be an earthquake, run!

195
00:09:06,340 --> 00:09:09,340
Look over there!

196
00:09:15,220 --> 00:09:16,860
It's Gorillamon! Move!

197
00:09:19,040 --> 00:09:21,937
Watch out for his energy cannon
attack, it'll drive you bananas!

198
00:09:22,020 --> 00:09:23,373
He's got a dark spiral!

199
00:09:23,600 --> 00:09:27,477
I thought that the dark spirals only
worked on ultimate level Digimon.

200
00:09:27,560 --> 00:09:31,577
If they can control champion level Digimon
too, then there must be different kinds.

201
00:09:31,660 --> 00:09:32,880
Uruji-Tarun!

202
00:09:52,940 --> 00:09:54,020
Heads up!

203
00:09:55,020 --> 00:09:56,780
Uruji-Tarun! No!

204
00:10:00,580 --> 00:10:01,410
Ah!

205
00:10:04,280 --> 00:10:05,897
Digitamamon tried to protect us.

206
00:10:05,980 --> 00:10:06,997
Why would he do that?

207
00:10:07,080 --> 00:10:08,668
Get here before he gets us!

208
00:10:08,820 --> 00:10:09,650
Whoa!

209
00:10:10,140 --> 00:10:10,970
Neemon, now!

210
00:10:11,100 --> 00:10:12,982
Please, allow me to handle this.

211
00:10:13,760 --> 00:10:15,440
Okay, Betamon? Okay!

212
00:10:19,760 --> 00:10:20,590
Digimon.

213
00:10:24,780 --> 00:10:26,300
Betamon, Digimon, too!

214
00:10:27,620 --> 00:10:28,450
Digimon?

215
00:10:30,980 --> 00:10:31,810
Seadramon!

216
00:10:34,060 --> 00:10:34,960
Wow, Michael!

217
00:10:35,360 --> 00:10:36,577
Zedramon's your Digimon!

218
00:10:36,660 --> 00:10:40,660
I still get chills remembering his
ice blast and ice winder attacks!

219
00:10:46,340 --> 00:10:49,222
Now that they're in the
water, Seadramon will win!

220
00:11:00,360 --> 00:11:01,800
Under deep carbon!

221
00:11:04,900 --> 00:11:06,180
Ice blast!

222
00:11:12,360 --> 00:11:13,480
He's in trouble!

223
00:11:13,800 --> 00:11:16,918
Okay, Palmon, you better
digivolve and help Seadramon!

224
00:11:17,040 --> 00:11:17,870
Ready when you are!

225
00:11:17,953 --> 00:11:18,783
Digimon!

226
00:11:20,560 --> 00:11:22,160
Palmon, digivolve too!

227
00:11:22,520 --> 00:11:24,277
Oh, Seadramon, time for that champion!

228
00:11:24,360 --> 00:11:25,190
Seadramon!

229
00:11:25,580 --> 00:11:26,410
Seadramon!

230
00:11:31,800 --> 00:11:32,800
Lightspeed Jemmy!

231
00:11:38,160 --> 00:11:39,440
Tokomon, you did it!

232
00:11:41,440 --> 00:11:42,540
Victory at last!

233
00:11:44,000 --> 00:11:45,657
Sorry we had to treat you so rough,

234
00:11:45,740 --> 00:11:48,257
but it was the only way to
get that Dark Spiral off you.

235
00:11:48,340 --> 00:11:51,597
You should be safe from now on, but
stay away from the Digimon Emperor.

236
00:11:51,680 --> 00:11:52,510
Thanks!

237
00:11:53,700 --> 00:11:57,257
Without that Dark Spiral, he doesn't
seem like a bad little monkey after all.

238
00:11:57,340 --> 00:11:59,317
I don't think any Digimon is born evil,

239
00:11:59,400 --> 00:12:01,077
but when they get those
dark spirals on them,

240
00:12:01,160 --> 00:12:03,057
they're not responsible for their actions.

241
00:12:03,140 --> 00:12:04,237
How do you get them?

242
00:12:04,320 --> 00:12:06,457
Remember when I told you
about the Digimon Emperor?

243
00:12:06,540 --> 00:12:08,997
He captures the Digimon
and makes them his slaves.

244
00:12:09,080 --> 00:12:09,910
Hmm.

245
00:12:10,380 --> 00:12:11,520
I can't believe it.

246
00:12:11,800 --> 00:12:14,157
Why would a young kid want to
take over the digital world

247
00:12:14,240 --> 00:12:16,877
when he could be playing polo
or practicing the violin?

248
00:12:16,960 --> 00:12:18,157
To him, it's a hobby.

249
00:12:18,240 --> 00:12:20,517
Do you want to know what
my hobby is, Michael?

250
00:12:20,600 --> 00:12:21,953
Boys don't count, Yoli.

251
00:12:22,260 --> 00:12:23,180
Who asked you?

252
00:12:24,980 --> 00:12:26,700
